    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.splitjoin\n\n### Description\n\nHi,\r\n\r\nI was not able to figure if it was possible to do this already based on the docs and help. If I have a function like this:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef something(a, b, c):\r\n    pass\r\n```\r\n\r\nand my cursor is on `something`, pressing `gS` does not split or join the arguments. The cursor has to be within the brackets. Is there a way to match the next (or previous) bracket on the line and use this for the split/join?\r\n\r\nThank you!",
    "closed_at": "2023-09-30T05:00:16Z",
